Subject: [PATCH 1/2] =?UTF-8?q?feat(migrate):=20add=20per-module=20collisi?=
 =?UTF-8?q?on=20alias=20hints=20to=20v3=E2=86=92v4=20codemod=20(issue=20#9?=
 =?UTF-8?q?11,=20Step=203)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When an adopter imports a collision symbol (e.g. `Account`, `Creative`,
`Sort`) directly from a `generated_poc` submodule, the codemod now
knows which module they're reaching into and emits the exact qualified
alias from `adcp.types` in the `after` field of each `flag_private`
finding — replacing the generic "private module" message with an
immediately actionable hint.

Changes:
- Add `GENERATED_POC_COLLISION_SYMBOL_MAP: dict[tuple[str, str], str]`
  with 38 entries covering 11 collision groups (Account, Authentication,
  Creative, CreditLimit, DeclaredBy, GovernanceAgent, MediaBuy, Setup,
  Signal, Sort, Unit).
- Update `_GENERATED_POC_FROM_IMPORT` regex to capture the module suffix
  in group(1) and the symbol list in group(2).
- Rewrite the `flag_private` detection block in `scan_file()` to look up
  `(module_suffix, symbol)` in the collision map and emit the precise
  qualified alias; collision findings are always `flag_private` (never
  auto-applied) because usage sites need renaming too.
- Update pre-pass and auto-apply section to use the new group numbering.
- Add 5 new tests: collision map API-coverage guard, per-module hint
  correctness (Account→CoreAccount, Creative→ListCreativesCreative),
  multi-module hint correctness, and never-auto-applied assertion.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
